WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:01:51.340 --> 00:01:56.220
<b>Impasse</b>

3
00:02:01.560 --> 00:02:04.190
[FAMILY A]
Hey! Somebody
go buy some more food!

4
00:02:04.220 --> 00:02:06.090
[FAMILY B]
Yeah!
We've got the money!

5
00:02:06.130 --> 00:02:08.730
[FAMILY C]
Get some more
booze while you're at it!

6
00:02:12.400 --> 00:02:15.200
When it comes to painting,
I'm in a league of my own!

7
00:02:15.240 --> 00:02:16.800
So, what do you think?

8
00:02:22.040 --> 00:02:22.940
M-My goggles!

9
00:02:26.800 --> 00:02:29.270
[USOPP]
They took all of the money.

10
00:02:30.140 --> 00:02:36.480
How can I face the
others now, Nami?

11
00:02:37.310 --> 00:02:39.850
All right, guys, it's time to kick their
asses.

12
00:02:39.880 --> 00:02:41.450
All of them!

13
00:02:47.390 --> 00:02:49.180
[KIDROCK]
That's it! Show 'em!

14
00:02:49.180 --> 00:02:50.450
Looks like you
lose this round!

15
00:02:50.480 --> 00:02:52.370
Losers get to go
pick up more booze!

16
00:02:52.370 --> 00:02:54.180
Buy all the food they
have in the shop, too!

17
00:02:54.210 --> 00:02:56.310
It's not like we
don't have the money!

18
00:02:56.390 --> 00:02:59.220
[laughter]

19
00:03:00.990 --> 00:03:02.160
Be right back.

20
00:03:03.830 --> 00:03:05.760
And when I am, I'm gonna win every hand.

21
00:03:05.800 --> 00:03:07.500
Just you wait!

22
00:03:13.360 --> 00:03:14.560
Hmm?

23
00:03:17.530 --> 00:03:18.740
Ahh!

24
00:03:27.740 --> 00:03:29.580
[RAZ-BERET]
What was that?
What happened?!

25
00:03:33.520 --> 00:03:35.420
Who the hell are those guys?

26
00:03:35.450 --> 00:03:37.820
You jerks! You got a death wish?

27
00:03:44.380 --> 00:03:46.220
I recognize them!

28
00:03:56.160 --> 00:03:58.260
It's that pirate.

29
00:03:58.340 --> 00:04:00.780
Straw Hat Luffy!

30
00:04:08.340 --> 00:04:11.240
Ha ha ha!

31
00:04:12.480 --> 00:04:15.210
So you came here to get
your money back, did ya?

32
00:04:15.250 --> 00:04:16.280
Bad move.

33
00:04:16.320 --> 00:04:18.150
Just take a
look around you.

34
00:04:18.180 --> 00:04:19.480
Do you really think the four

35
00:04:19.520 --> 00:04:22.250
of you are enough
to handle all of us?

36
00:04:22.290 --> 00:04:25.060
Ha ha ha!

37
00:04:25.090 --> 00:04:26.620
But, since you're here,

38
00:04:26.660 --> 00:04:27.690
we might as well

39
00:04:27.780 --> 00:04:30.520
take those big bounties
you've got on your heads.

40
00:04:31.360 --> 00:04:33.430
He's the captain of
that long-nosed weakling

41
00:04:33.460 --> 00:04:35.170
we took care of earlier.

42
00:04:35.200 --> 00:04:36.230
[laughter]

43
00:04:36.270 --> 00:04:37.940
With that pitiful excuse
for a pirate on his crew,

44
00:04:38.020 --> 00:04:40.560
he can't possibly
be that strong.

45
00:04:43.930 --> 00:04:46.330
Let's go! C'mon, shrimp!

46
00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:50.200
Now, Gum Gum...

47
00:04:51.350 --> 00:04:52.850
Huh?

48
00:04:55.280 --> 00:04:56.880
What do you think you're doing?

49
00:04:56.910 --> 00:04:57.610
Hahaha!

50
00:04:57.640 --> 00:04:58.610
Are you punching him?

51
00:04:58.650 --> 00:05:01.320
Not even a bombardment
from battleship cannons

52
00:05:01.350 --> 00:05:02.950
can put a dent in that armor.

53
00:05:03.500 --> 00:05:04.700
Hahaha! What a joke!

54
00:05:06.950 --> 00:05:08.650
If you're just
gonna play around,

55
00:05:08.680 --> 00:05:11.760
then I'll go ahead
and end this right now.

56
00:05:27.800 --> 00:05:29.300
And Cannon!

57
00:05:36.550 --> 00:05:40.680
[cries of surprise]

58
00:05:43.250 --> 00:05:45.690
[POLKA-HAT]
He punched
a hole right through it!

59
00:05:46.950 --> 00:05:48.160
[ZAMBAI]
Hey!

60
00:05:48.570 --> 00:05:50.600
Hold on! W-Wait a
second, you guys!

61
00:05:50.640 --> 00:05:53.170
Let's talk about this first!

62
00:05:54.240 --> 00:05:57.080
[ZAMBAI]
Okay? Guys?

63
00:05:57.080 --> 00:05:59.280
Okay, guys,
fire the cannons!

64
00:06:03.250 --> 00:06:07.090
Now, Three-Sword
Style Kara Suma...

65
00:06:12.980 --> 00:06:14.340
...Raven Hunt!

66
00:06:27.520 --> 00:06:28.570
What?! Impossible!

67
00:06:28.570 --> 00:06:30.970
Those cannonballs
are made of iron!

68
00:06:36.490 --> 00:06:37.790
The cannons, too?!

69
00:06:39.640 --> 00:06:41.080
[GOLDILOCKS]
Holy crap!

70
00:06:41.350 --> 00:06:43.420
These guys are seriously bad news!

71
00:06:44.240 --> 00:06:45.580
[PURPLE SHIRT]
Let's get out of here!

72
00:06:45.610 --> 00:06:47.580
Everybody run
for the back door!

73
00:06:55.580 --> 00:06:57.590
You guys started this fight.

74
00:06:57.660 --> 00:07:00.770
It's kind of pathetic to run from it like
cowards.

75
00:07:00.800 --> 00:07:02.970
Party Table...

76
00:07:03.000 --> 00:07:05.270
...Kick Course!

77
00:07:18.360 --> 00:07:19.860
We... We can't make
it to the backdoor!

78
00:07:20.090 --> 00:07:22.500
Windows! Use the windows!

79
00:07:23.250 --> 00:07:24.380
[CHOPPER]
Rumble!

80
00:07:25.720 --> 00:07:27.230
Horn Point!

81
00:07:37.470 --> 00:07:39.710
Roseo Colonnade!

82
00:07:45.930 --> 00:07:49.000
Wait! Wait, wait, wait,
wait, wait, you guys!

83
00:07:49.040 --> 00:07:49.940
It's the money, right?

84
00:07:49.970 --> 00:07:51.170
You just want the money back?

85
00:07:51.190 --> 00:07:55.490
The 200 million berries the
long-nosed guy had? Is that it?

86
00:07:55.520 --> 00:07:56.760
I'm sorry to be
the one to tell you,

87
00:07:56.790 --> 00:07:58.960
but that pile of money
isn't here anymore.

88
00:07:59.000 --> 00:08:00.600
Franky, the family
boss, took all of it

89
00:08:00.630 --> 00:08:02.370
and went out on
a shopping spree!

90
00:08:02.380 --> 00:08:03.880
And since he's buying
something on the black market,

91
00:08:03.910 --> 00:08:05.720
we don't have any idea
where he might be

92
00:08:05.750 --> 00:08:07.920
or even how to find him!

93
00:08:07.950 --> 00:08:09.990
So, no matter how much
of a rampage you go on,

94
00:08:10.010 --> 00:08:12.310
that 200 million
won't be coming back!

95
00:08:12.310 --> 00:08:13.680
So why don't you an...

96
00:08:15.350 --> 00:08:18.020
Zambai!

97
00:08:18.050 --> 00:08:20.860
Shut up. That's
enough out of you.

98
00:08:20.860 --> 00:08:23.760
This has nothing to do with the money.

99
00:08:23.790 --> 00:08:26.990
Damn straight.
It's too late for that.

100
00:08:31.630 --> 00:08:34.370
Not even your bones will be left when
we're done.

101
00:08:34.740 --> 00:08:36.350
Not even our bones?!

102
00:08:36.540 --> 00:08:37.300
What's the matter with you?

103
00:08:37.370 --> 00:08:38.800
Acting like a
bunch of cowards!

104
00:08:38.850 --> 00:08:40.150
We're the Franky Family!

105
00:08:40.180 --> 00:08:42.560
We're the ones who do all the
bone breaking around here!

106
00:08:42.590 --> 00:08:44.760
Got it? Never
forget who you are!

107
00:08:44.790 --> 00:08:45.820
Okay, brothers!

108
00:08:45.860 --> 00:08:48.930
Let's show 'em the specialty
of The Franky House!

109
00:08:54.000 --> 00:08:57.700
Now! Fire the
Anything Shot Cannon!

110
00:09:03.900 --> 00:09:05.740
[BEARDFACE]
Here they come! Attack!

111
00:09:06.840 --> 00:09:09.510
Keep firing until there's
nothing left to shoot!

112
00:09:11.790 --> 00:09:13.820
[GIANT SPIKE]
Come on!
There're only four of them!

113
00:09:18.150 --> 00:09:18.850
[CITIZENS]
– Huh?
– Huh?

114
00:09:18.850 --> 00:09:19.720
[FRANKY]
Huh?

115
00:09:33.030 --> 00:09:35.000
[CITIZEN C]
What was that? Fireworks?

116
00:09:35.030 --> 00:09:35.800
[CITIZEN D]
Sounds like it's coming

117
00:09:35.830 --> 00:09:37.970
from out toward
The Franky House.

118
00:09:38.870 --> 00:09:40.400
Them again?

119
00:09:40.440 --> 00:09:41.980
What trouble are they up to this time?

120
00:09:41.980 --> 00:09:43.520
I know, right?

121
00:09:43.550 --> 00:09:45.790
Hey! Quiet, they're
gonna hear us!

122
00:09:48.690 --> 00:09:49.760
[MOZU]
Oh, boy.

123
00:09:49.800 --> 00:09:51.540
Sounds like they're getting a little
carried away.

124
00:09:51.570 --> 00:09:53.510
[KIWI]
When those boys party.

125
00:09:53.530 --> 00:09:56.670
They really don't show
any restraint, now do they?

126
00:09:56.700 --> 00:09:59.700
[FRANKY]
No big deal. It's not
like they do it all the time.

127
00:09:59.740 --> 00:10:04.570
It's a nice day. Hahaha!

128
00:10:18.290 --> 00:10:20.300
[SANJI]
Should we go after Franky?

129
00:10:20.420 --> 00:10:22.260
And start looking where?

130
00:10:23.390 --> 00:10:24.930
Ah, man, looks like these idiots

131
00:10:24.960 --> 00:10:28.760
really didn't know
where he took the money.

132
00:10:28.800 --> 00:10:29.830
[SANJI]
And if we do find him.

133
00:10:29.860 --> 00:10:33.000
If he spent it, then
there's no getting it back.

134
00:10:35.420 --> 00:10:36.120
What now? Even if we
wait around for him,

135
00:10:36.120 --> 00:10:37.740
he might not be
back for quite a while.

136
00:10:37.740 --> 00:10:40.370
Okay! The first aid
treatment is all done!

137
00:10:40.400 --> 00:10:41.870
We need to take him
back on a stretcher,

138
00:10:43.210 --> 00:10:44.910
so I could use
some help over here!

139
00:10:44.910 --> 00:10:46.740
Hanging around here won't do any good.

140
00:10:46.780 --> 00:10:48.610
Let's head back to the ship for now.

141
00:10:48.650 --> 00:10:51.220
We left Nami there
all by herself

142
00:10:51.230 --> 00:10:53.900
and Robin's still missing.

143
00:10:53.930 --> 00:10:55.960
The ship's a problem, too.

144
00:10:56.000 --> 00:10:56.960
[ZORO]
Yeah.

145
00:10:57.210 --> 00:10:58.560
Hey, Luffy!

146
00:11:02.600 --> 00:11:03.400
[LUFFY]
I've made a decision.

147
00:11:03.400 --> 00:11:04.700
Huh?

148
00:11:05.470 --> 00:11:07.140
About the ship.

149
00:11:16.310 --> 00:11:19.150
It's time to part
ways with the Merry.

150
00:11:19.180 --> 00:11:21.280
We'll say goodbye to her here.

151
00:11:24.830 --> 00:11:28.750
<b>Galley-La Company
Headquarters</b>

152
00:11:28.260 --> 00:11:32.160
[USOPP]
Don't be
ridiculous! You're lying!

153
00:11:32.160 --> 00:11:33.730
That man is
seriously stubborn!

154
00:11:33.760 --> 00:11:35.500
It's infuriating!

155
00:11:36.270 --> 00:11:37.800
We don't even know
if he has it or not,

156
00:11:37.830 --> 00:11:39.700
yet they keep
sending me out here.

157
00:11:39.740 --> 00:11:40.970
Over and over again.

158
00:11:41.060 --> 00:11:43.550
I wish those people would put themselves
in my shoes for once.

159
00:11:49.200 --> 00:11:50.400
It's Kalifa.

160
00:11:50.400 --> 00:11:52.520
[ICEBURG]
Mwell, come in.

161
00:11:53.940 --> 00:11:55.570
You must be worn out, Sir.

162
00:11:55.610 --> 00:11:57.440
Would you like something to drink?

163
00:11:58.010 --> 00:12:00.110
[ICEBURG]
I would. Thank you.

164
00:12:01.480 --> 00:12:03.280
[ICEBURG]
Maybe some tea.

165
00:12:03.390 --> 00:12:04.870
[KALIFA]
I've already prepared it.

166
00:12:06.080 --> 00:12:09.080
Mwell, I'd expect
nothing less from you.

167
00:12:09.120 --> 00:12:11.020
Thank you. I'm grateful.

168
00:12:13.460 --> 00:12:17.090
Poor Mr. Corgy is always so
angry when he leaves, isn't he?

169
00:12:17.130 --> 00:12:19.360
What in the world does he come here to
talk about?

170
00:12:19.400 --> 00:12:20.920
[ICEBURG]
Oh, that.

171
00:12:20.920 --> 00:12:23.190
Those he represents
want something I have,

172
00:12:23.220 --> 00:12:25.220
and they keep
making various offers.

173
00:12:27.260 --> 00:12:30.100
It must be something of great importance
then, isn't it?

174
00:12:30.130 --> 00:12:32.200
Mwell, maybe so,

175
00:12:32.230 --> 00:12:35.340
though I always deny
knowing anything about it.

176
00:12:35.370 --> 00:12:38.300
They really are tiresome people.

177
00:12:43.060 --> 00:12:46.200
Hey! Usopp's finally
awake, you guys!

178
00:12:46.230 --> 00:12:48.970
All right! Good to hear!

179
00:12:49.000 --> 00:12:49.840
[NAMI sighs]

180
00:12:49.870 --> 00:12:52.100
That's one less thing to worry about.

181
00:12:55.360 --> 00:12:56.630
[LUFFY]
Hey, Usopp!

182
00:13:00.980 --> 00:13:05.050
[SANJI]
Huh... Robin
still isn't back yet.

183
00:13:05.980 --> 00:13:06.950
[NAMI]
You know,

184
00:13:06.980 --> 00:13:09.720
I oughta punch you for
scaring us like that!

185
00:13:10.790 --> 00:13:11.970
Yeah, no kidding.

186
00:13:11.970 --> 00:13:13.970
Though it looks like you've
taken enough punches already,

187
00:13:14.000 --> 00:13:15.070
if you ask me.

188
00:13:15.110 --> 00:13:18.740
What were you thinking
taking those guys on alone?

189
00:13:18.830 --> 00:13:21.170
You can't just run off and fight whoever
you want.

190
00:13:21.200 --> 00:13:23.260
[ZORO]
Oh that's a good
one, coming from you!

191
00:13:23.260 --> 00:13:25.160
[LUFFY]
Hahahaha!

192
00:13:25.190 --> 00:13:27.890
This wouldn't have happened if I was
strong like you guys.

193
00:13:27.930 --> 00:13:29.730
I'm sorry.

194
00:13:29.760 --> 00:13:31.260
It's all my fault.

195
00:13:31.400 --> 00:13:33.800
I'm so ashamed of myself.

196
00:13:38.790 --> 00:13:42.160
Hey, hey, stop! I get it!
I know you're sorry,

197
00:13:42.190 --> 00:13:44.790
but you don't have to get
all touchy, feely on me okay?!

198
00:13:44.880 --> 00:13:46.050
[USOPP]
But all our savings!

199
00:13:46.080 --> 00:13:47.520
All that trouble
we went through!

200
00:13:47.550 --> 00:13:49.220
What about the Merry?

201
00:13:49.300 --> 00:13:52.040
Take it easy! You shouldn't
be out of bed yet!

202
00:13:52.070 --> 00:13:53.340
C'mon, calm down.

203
00:13:53.370 --> 00:13:56.170
Stop your whining and listen to the
doctor!

204
00:13:57.540 --> 00:14:00.120
[USOPP]
So is there a chance

205
00:14:00.120 --> 00:14:02.490
we might get our
money back after all?

206
00:14:02.520 --> 00:14:04.090
Well, maybe.

207
00:14:04.110 --> 00:14:07.920
We won't know for sure
'til that Franky guy shows up.

208
00:14:07.950 --> 00:14:10.490
I see. I'm sorry.

209
00:14:10.520 --> 00:14:12.420
Hey, even if we can't
get the rest back,

210
00:14:12.460 --> 00:14:16.730
we still have a hundred million
berries left over! Don't worry!

211
00:14:16.770 --> 00:14:19.010
Hahahahaha!

212
00:14:19.040 --> 00:14:21.840
[NAMI]
Yeah, but he
lost twice that much!

213
00:14:21.840 --> 00:14:22.540
[CHOPPER]
Nami.

214
00:14:22.540 --> 00:14:24.980
[NAMI]
Eh. Sorry, Usopp.

215
00:14:25.010 --> 00:14:27.250
No, it's fine.

216
00:14:27.280 --> 00:14:31.320
More importantly, is
Merry gonna be okay?

217
00:14:31.320 --> 00:14:35.190
I mean, can we get her repaired
with the money we have left?

218
00:14:35.220 --> 00:14:36.920
We're lucky we have all
these awesome shipwrights

219
00:14:36.960 --> 00:14:37.990
to work on her.

220
00:14:38.020 --> 00:14:39.960
But I know things are
gonna get rough out there,

221
00:14:39.990 --> 00:14:43.130
so I want her to be
stronger than ever before.

222
00:14:43.160 --> 00:14:44.830
We gotta do a lot more
than just a little touch up.

223
00:14:44.830 --> 00:14:45.830
We decided to get a new ship instead.

224
00:14:45.830 --> 00:14:47.570
Eh?

225
00:14:47.600 --> 00:14:49.770
I know that we probably
should've asked you first

226
00:14:49.800 --> 00:14:51.700
but we didn't have much choice.

227
00:14:51.740 --> 00:14:53.510
Either way, I've made up my mind.

228
00:14:53.540 --> 00:14:55.680
The Going Merry has
taken good care of us.

229
00:14:55.710 --> 00:14:59.310
But it looks like our journey
with her has to end here.

230
00:15:07.650 --> 00:15:08.760
[LUFFY]
Anyway.

231
00:15:09.310 --> 00:15:12.380
Ice Pops gave us this awesome
ship catalogue to flip through.

232
00:15:12.410 --> 00:15:14.780
There's all kinds of different
ships we could pick from here.

233
00:15:14.820 --> 00:15:17.050
And if we decided to
shop for a used model.

234
00:15:17.080 --> 00:15:18.850
We could go bigger
than the Merry.

235
00:15:18.920 --> 00:15:21.090
And still keep our budget
under a hundred million.

236
00:15:21.120 --> 00:15:22.990
[USOPP]
Wait.

237
00:15:23.090 --> 00:15:24.290
Just stop.

238
00:15:24.290 --> 00:15:29.430
I get it, Luffy but the joke's
gone on long enough, okay? See?

239
00:15:29.460 --> 00:15:31.130
Chopper doesn't
know you're kidding!

240
00:15:31.140 --> 00:15:33.710
Look how upset
this is making him!

241
00:15:33.730 --> 00:15:35.360
Jeez, Captain, you
should know better

242
00:15:35.420 --> 00:15:37.120
than to treat
your crew like that!

243
00:15:37.140 --> 00:15:39.610
Come on, Nami,
back me up here.

244
00:15:43.880 --> 00:15:45.790
Hold up does
that mean we,

245
00:15:45.820 --> 00:15:48.660
we don't have enough for the repairs?

246
00:15:48.690 --> 00:15:51.600
It's 'cause I lost the
200 million, isn't it?

247
00:15:51.630 --> 00:15:53.530
And now we can't afford the work on the
Merry.

248
00:15:53.560 --> 00:15:54.900
Is that what this is about?

249
00:15:54.930 --> 00:15:55.960
After all,

250
00:15:56.000 --> 00:15:58.570
a first-class shipyard is
gonna cost a lot, right?

251
00:15:58.600 --> 00:16:00.500
Would you stop
and listen to me?!

252
00:16:00.630 --> 00:16:03.200
What is it?! Tell me!

253
00:16:03.270 --> 00:16:04.870
Don't try to sugarcoat it!

254
00:16:04.900 --> 00:16:06.140
I'm not, okay?!

255
00:16:06.170 --> 00:16:09.140
I don't even care that you lost
all the money, that's over now!

256
00:16:09.170 --> 00:16:10.340
If that's how you feel,

257
00:16:10.370 --> 00:16:12.110
then what's with all this
crap about buying a new ship?!

258
00:16:12.140 --> 00:16:13.580
Both of you, stop it!

259
00:16:13.600 --> 00:16:15.570
Fighting isn't gonna help.

260
00:16:15.600 --> 00:16:17.600
Just calm down for a sec!

261
00:16:18.470 --> 00:16:19.770
I don't see what
I'm doing wrong!

262
00:16:19.800 --> 00:16:21.740
He's the one saying
all this dumb stuff!

263
00:16:21.770 --> 00:16:22.740
[NAMI]
I know how you feel,

264
00:16:22.890 --> 00:16:25.660
but you shouldn't get
so worked up right now.

265
00:16:25.740 --> 00:16:26.880
Listen to Nami, Usopp,

266
00:16:26.910 --> 00:16:29.850
if you don't get any rest,
you're not gonna get better!

267
00:16:29.900 --> 00:16:31.170
Who cares about me?!

268
00:16:31.170 --> 00:16:33.010
How can you just sit here
when he's making jokes

269
00:16:33.040 --> 00:16:34.710
about getting a new ship?

270
00:16:34.740 --> 00:16:36.110
I'm not joking about anything,

271
00:16:36.140 --> 00:16:38.170
this was a hard
decision for me, too!

272
00:16:38.210 --> 00:16:41.480
Oh yeah, I feel really sorry for you!

273
00:16:41.500 --> 00:16:43.700
Already window-shopping
for a new toy!

274
00:16:45.000 --> 00:16:46.670
You trying to pick
a fight with me?!

275
00:16:46.700 --> 00:16:48.610
I don't want your damn pity, got it?

276
00:16:48.640 --> 00:16:50.710
If you tell me it doesn't
matter that I lost the money,

277
00:16:50.740 --> 00:16:53.510
then why are you talking
about buying a new ship?

278
00:16:53.540 --> 00:16:55.010
Just spit it out already.

279
00:16:55.050 --> 00:16:57.120
If we can't afford the
repairs 'cause I screwed up,

280
00:16:57.150 --> 00:16:57.920
then tell me!

281
00:16:57.950 --> 00:16:59.590
Don't show me some
stupid catalogue

282
00:16:59.590 --> 00:17:03.560
and change the subject!
I wanna know the truth!

283
00:17:03.590 --> 00:17:04.820
The Merry can't be...

284
00:17:04.930 --> 00:17:08.530
[loud wave crash
covers dialogue]

285
00:17:16.800 --> 00:17:20.220
[USOPP]
Wha... What did you just say?

286
00:17:20.860 --> 00:17:23.020
[LUFFY]
Don't make me repeat myself.

287
00:17:23.450 --> 00:17:26.800
I told you, the Merry
can't be repaired any more.

288
00:17:26.930 --> 00:17:32.070
No matter what we do,
we... we can't fix her.

289
00:17:32.160 --> 00:17:35.830
Otherwise I wouldn't
say something like that.

290
00:17:35.860 --> 00:17:36.930
You mean this ship?

291
00:17:37.000 --> 00:17:39.930
This ship that we're riding
on right now is broken?

292
00:17:39.960 --> 00:17:40.930
[LUFFY]
That's right.

293
00:17:40.930 --> 00:17:46.470
It's only a matter of
time before she sinks.

294
00:17:46.500 --> 00:17:48.870
What're you talking
about Luffy? That's nuts.

295
00:17:48.940 --> 00:17:50.450
[LUFFY]
No, I'm serious.

296
00:17:50.480 --> 00:17:53.820
The shipwrights took a look
at the Merry themselves.

297
00:17:53.890 --> 00:17:57.000
They said she wouldn't even hold out until
the next island.

298
00:17:57.240 --> 00:17:59.980
[LUFFY]
And it's settled? So that's it?

299
00:18:00.010 --> 00:18:02.110
A bunch of strangers tell
you to scrap your ship

300
00:18:02.140 --> 00:18:04.110
and you don't even
ask any questions?

301
00:18:04.130 --> 00:18:05.930
[LUFFY]
That's enough.

302
00:18:05.960 --> 00:18:07.500
[USOPP]
I understand
that these guys know

303
00:18:07.530 --> 00:18:08.230
what they're talking about,

304
00:18:08.230 --> 00:18:11.200
but this is just wrong.

305
00:18:11.270 --> 00:18:13.540
Don't give up on the Merry!

306
00:18:13.570 --> 00:18:15.900
What about all the adventures we've gone
on together?

307
00:18:15.900 --> 00:18:18.040
What about all the
battles we've fought?!

308
00:18:18.050 --> 00:18:21.480
She's our friend!
She's one of us!

309
00:18:21.520 --> 00:18:23.690
Are you gonna abandon
her for another ship

310
00:18:23.720 --> 00:18:25.990
without a second thought?!

311
00:18:28.950 --> 00:18:31.450
After all we've been
through is that how little

312
00:18:31.460 --> 00:18:33.930
the Merry means to you, Luffy?

313
00:18:36.900 --> 00:18:40.010
I know you're upset Usopp,
but you need to calm down.

314
00:18:40.040 --> 00:18:42.110
[USOPP]
Sorry, but no.

315
00:18:42.940 --> 00:18:46.080
I'm not backing
down 'til we settle this.

316
00:18:46.110 --> 00:18:47.650
Usopp, please.

317
00:18:49.920 --> 00:18:53.620
What? So you know
better than the shipwrights?

318
00:18:53.720 --> 00:18:56.590
If we had someone on the
crew who knew about this stuff,

319
00:18:56.620 --> 00:18:58.820
we wouldn't have asked
them in the first place!

320
00:18:58.850 --> 00:18:59.890
Then forget them!

321
00:18:59.920 --> 00:19:02.860
We don't need those
guys telling us what to do.

322
00:19:02.890 --> 00:19:05.800
I'll repair the Merry
myself, just like before!

323
00:19:05.830 --> 00:19:06.790
We've made it this far,

324
00:19:06.790 --> 00:19:09.060
so there's no reason why
we can't go on that way.

325
00:19:09.090 --> 00:19:11.090
Here, I'll get
started right now.

326
00:19:11.120 --> 00:19:12.860
C'mon guys, help me out.

327
00:19:12.890 --> 00:19:14.730
That's not gonna work.

328
00:19:14.760 --> 00:19:17.130
That's right, we don't
have enough lumber do we?

329
00:19:17.370 --> 00:19:19.400
I'd better go buy
some at the shipyard.

330
00:19:19.440 --> 00:19:21.240
We've got a lotta work to do.

331
00:19:21.270 --> 00:19:23.940
You're not a shipwright,
Usopp, you hear me?!

332
00:19:23.980 --> 00:19:25.680
Stop it, Luffy!

333
00:19:26.140 --> 00:19:27.780
[USOPP]
Yeah, you're right! I know.

334
00:19:27.810 --> 00:19:28.580
But so what?!

335
00:19:28.580 --> 00:19:29.520
I don't see why
you're so hung up

336
00:19:30.800 --> 00:19:32.480
on everything those
stupid shipwrights say!

337
00:19:32.480 --> 00:19:33.450
If they knew what
she'd gone through

338
00:19:33.480 --> 00:19:35.680
they wouldn't give up
on the Merry so easy!

339
00:19:35.770 --> 00:19:37.200
They just want your money!

340
00:19:37.320 --> 00:19:38.600
[NAMI]
Usopp.

341
00:19:38.600 --> 00:19:39.640
[USOPP]
The Merry's our ship,

342
00:19:39.670 --> 00:19:40.770
so it's our job to take care

343
00:19:40.800 --> 00:19:43.610
of her without
someone else butting in!

344
00:19:43.640 --> 00:19:45.040
I'm not giving up.

345
00:19:45.080 --> 00:19:49.080
I won't let them take
the Merry away from me!

346
00:19:49.110 --> 00:19:50.780
This is stupid.

347
00:19:50.810 --> 00:19:52.250
You got fooled by
a bunch of salesmen

348
00:19:52.280 --> 00:19:54.680
trying to pawn off a used boat.

349
00:19:54.780 --> 00:19:56.080
The Luffy I know
wouldn't cave in

350
00:19:56.110 --> 00:19:58.550
to some sales pitch
from a total stranger!

351
00:19:58.610 --> 00:20:00.580
He'd believe in the
strength of the Merry

352
00:20:00.620 --> 00:20:02.720
and the strength of his crew!

353
00:20:02.750 --> 00:20:03.720
But here you are, acting like

354
00:20:03.760 --> 00:20:06.820
you know everything and
ignoring your friends!

355
00:20:06.860 --> 00:20:09.860
I can't believe that's the kind of captain
you turned out to be!

356
00:20:09.900 --> 00:20:12.330
I thought you were better than that!

357
00:20:12.340 --> 00:20:14.610
You're not being fair,
Usopp. Luffy felt the...

358
00:20:14.640 --> 00:20:18.080
You stay out of this!
It was my call. I stand by it.

359
00:20:18.120 --> 00:20:19.780
There's nothing you can do.

360
00:20:19.800 --> 00:20:22.600
We're getting a new ship
whether you like it or not.

361
00:20:22.610 --> 00:20:24.580
This is the end of
the road for the Merry!

362
00:20:24.610 --> 00:20:27.210
I'm not leaving her here.
I don't care what you say!

363
00:20:27.240 --> 00:20:29.550
I know you're always trying
to think about the future,

364
00:20:29.580 --> 00:20:31.820
but not everyone on
this crew is like that!

365
00:20:31.880 --> 00:20:33.950
I see the Merry as one
of our friends, got it?!

366
00:20:34.010 --> 00:20:36.010
And I won't abandon her when she's hurt!

367
00:20:36.080 --> 00:20:37.280
[LUFFY]
Don't be stupid!

368
00:20:37.320 --> 00:20:39.790
Even if she is a friend, that doesn't mean
she's a person!

369
00:20:39.920 --> 00:20:40.820
[USOPP]
She is to me!

370
00:20:40.850 --> 00:20:42.450
And she still has
the strength to live!

371
00:20:42.480 --> 00:20:43.680
But you wouldn't
appreciate that,

372
00:20:43.720 --> 00:20:46.030
'cause all you care about is
getting a new ship to play with!

373
00:20:46.030 --> 00:20:48.000
[SANJI]
All right, that's
enough, both of you!

374
00:20:48.080 --> 00:20:49.780
Just calm down and we
can settle this later!

375
00:20:49.820 --> 00:20:51.340
[LUFFY]
Would you listen to yourself?!

376
00:20:51.340 --> 00:20:52.570
Luffy!

377
00:20:52.580 --> 00:20:54.650
Don't act like you're the only
one who's torn up about this,

378
00:20:54.690 --> 00:20:56.090
we all feel the same way!

379
00:20:56.120 --> 00:20:57.060
If that was true,

380
00:20:57.090 --> 00:20:58.820
then you wouldn't be
looking for a new ship!

381
00:20:58.860 --> 00:20:59.960
All right, fine!

382
00:20:59.990 --> 00:21:01.660
If you don't like the way
your captain does things,

383
00:21:01.690 --> 00:21:03.760
why don't you go
ahead and get off...

384
00:21:07.130 --> 00:21:08.730
[CHOPPER]
Sanji!

385
00:21:14.710 --> 00:21:17.010
This is going way too far!

386
00:21:17.040 --> 00:21:19.250
What the hell is wrong with you?!

387
00:21:19.280 --> 00:21:20.280
If you don't watch it,

388
00:21:20.310 --> 00:21:22.050
you're gonna say something
you can't take back!

389
00:21:22.080 --> 00:21:23.680
So calm down!

390
00:21:30.650 --> 00:21:33.950
Yeah, I'm sorry. I don't
know what I was thinking.

391
00:21:33.990 --> 00:21:35.920
[USOPP]
You don't have to apologize.

392
00:21:35.950 --> 00:21:38.460
'Cause that's how you
really feel, isn't it?

393
00:21:38.490 --> 00:21:39.890
That's not true!

394
00:21:40.250 --> 00:21:41.520
Just get rid of your dead weight

395
00:21:43.900 --> 00:21:46.660
and move on before
they can slow you down.

396
00:21:48.360 --> 00:21:50.280
[USOPP]
If you're gonna
throw away the Merry,

397
00:21:50.840 --> 00:21:53.140
might as well
throw me away, too.

398
00:21:53.670 --> 00:21:57.010
I know you're pissed off but
don't say stupid crap like that.

399
00:21:57.040 --> 00:21:58.410
No, I'm serious.

400
00:21:58.440 --> 00:22:02.710
I've been thinking about this for a while
now.

401
00:22:02.750 --> 00:22:04.650
[USOPP]
It isn't like it was before.

402
00:22:04.680 --> 00:22:09.090
You guys are just too strong
for me. I can't keep up anymore.

403
00:22:09.120 --> 00:22:11.120
I mean, look at
what happened today.

404
00:22:11.240 --> 00:22:14.710
You can't even trust me with your money.

405
00:22:14.710 --> 00:22:15.910
There's no point
in keeping me around

406
00:22:15.970 --> 00:22:18.740
if all I do is
cause you trouble.

407
00:22:23.210 --> 00:22:26.620
You don't want weak people on your crew,
do you?

408
00:22:26.710 --> 00:22:27.910
Luffy,

409
00:22:27.940 --> 00:22:31.840
I still believe that you'll be
the King of Pirates one day.

410
00:22:31.860 --> 00:22:33.130
But as for me,

411
00:22:33.180 --> 00:22:36.920
I'm just lucky I was
able to make it this far.

412
00:22:36.950 --> 00:22:40.220
Even back when we first met and
I was going to set off alone,

413
00:22:40.240 --> 00:22:44.140
you probably just invited
me on your ship out of pity.

414
00:22:44.190 --> 00:22:45.890
[ZORO]
What are you talking about?

415
00:22:45.930 --> 00:22:46.830
Get on already!

416
00:22:46.900 --> 00:22:49.240
[LUFFY]
We're friends.
Right? So get on.

417
00:22:53.390 --> 00:22:55.360
That's the only reason I'm here.

418
00:22:57.460 --> 00:22:58.970
[USOPP]
There's no sense
in travelling together

419
00:22:59.000 --> 00:23:01.300
if we don't even
have the same goal!

420
00:23:03.080 --> 00:23:06.110
[SANJI]
Hey! Usopp,
where're you going?

421
00:23:06.780 --> 00:23:08.820
[USOPP]
Wherever I go,
it's my business.

422
00:23:09.200 --> 00:23:12.530
It has nothing to do with you anymore.

423
00:23:13.880 --> 00:23:15.850
Sorry guys.

424
00:23:18.380 --> 00:23:21.760
I'm leaving the crew.
This is goodbye.

425
00:23:23.990 --> 00:23:29.360
♪ dramatic music ♪

426
00:23:31.720 --> 00:23:35.390
Luffy, what's wrong? Please.

427
00:23:35.430 --> 00:23:37.460
You're the captain, aren't you?

428
00:23:41.670 --> 00:23:47.500
[NAMI]
Fine. Have it your way, then.

429
00:23:47.540 --> 00:23:49.810
Usopp!

430
00:23:49.840 --> 00:23:52.840
Get back here!
It shouldn't be like this!

431
00:23:52.880 --> 00:23:54.550
C'mon! We can talk!

432
00:23:54.570 --> 00:23:56.200
Yeah! Come back!

433
00:23:56.230 --> 00:23:58.300
I want you to stay!

434
00:23:58.340 --> 00:24:03.270
Don't leave us!

435
00:24:03.310 --> 00:24:06.080
[CHOPPER]
Usopp! Please!

436
00:24:06.110 --> 00:24:07.580
Say something.

437
00:24:16.750 --> 00:24:21.750
[USOPP]
Luffy. I'm sorry
I can't follow you anymore.

438
00:24:21.790 --> 00:24:24.620
And I'm sorry I was a
pain 'til the bitter end.

439
00:24:26.660 --> 00:24:28.660
[USOPP]
I know you're
the captain of this ship,

440
00:24:28.690 --> 00:24:32.830
so the Merry belongs to you.

441
00:24:32.860 --> 00:24:36.600
That's why I want you to
fight me, Monkey D. Luffy.

442
00:24:44.600 --> 00:24:47.010
[USOPP]
I challenge you to a duel!

443
00:24:53.880 --> 00:24:57.040
Huh? Whoa, wait!
What are you saying?!

444
00:24:59.320 --> 00:25:01.060
At ten o'clock tonight.

445
00:25:01.090 --> 00:25:05.030
I'll be back. So you better
be ready for a fight, Captain.

446
00:25:05.060 --> 00:25:08.260
I can't stop you from destroying
your own ship but if I win,

447
00:25:08.300 --> 00:25:10.970
I'm taking the
Merry and leaving.

448
00:25:11.000 --> 00:25:12.170
Either way.

449
00:25:12.200 --> 00:25:15.270
When we're done, the last bond
between us will be broken.
